              "line_start": 214,
              "line_end": 1284,
              "title": "LogViewerView has 2 disjoint cohesion groups",
              "issue": "Group A (TTY interaction): inputText, selectedOptionIdx, promptToolID — used exclusively by inputField, sendInput, permissionPrompt, askUserQuestionPrompt, planApprovalPrompt. Group B (display/rendering): agent, target, settings, stickyHeader, vm, showTaskPanel, sessionManager — used by all layout and rendering methods. The two groups share no variables except sessionManager (which is used in logHeader for the stop button and in Group A prompt methods for bridge access), but the concerns are structurally and functionally disjoint.",
              "impact": "A change in PTY/session interaction behavior (e.g., different key-code protocol, new prompt type) forces modification of the same struct that owns all display rendering. The struct spans 1070 lines and mixes two independently changeable concerns.",
