              "title": "LogViewerView performs 9+ distinct actions across 3 stakeholder domains",
              "issue": "The struct performs: resolves (bridge), evaluates (send eligibility), classifies (target type), formats (title/fonts), calculates (scroll height), renders (all message/tool/task UI), maps (role/tool/status to colors/icons), wires (task lifecycle), dispatches (prompt type), sends (TTY raw bytes). These span UX design (layout, colors), session interaction (PTY send, prompt handling), and tool-specific rendering (15+ tool type cases in toolExpandedContent at line 622).",
              "impact": "A UX designer, a session protocol engineer, and a tool-feature developer can independently require changes to the same struct. The 15-case toolExpandedContent dispatch (lines 622–708) grows with every new tool type, giving each tool team a reason to change this view.",
